# L §6.4 (round 8): a move the scenario declares books nothing before D, "LOAD-SCENARIO where load sees the day":
# extra's day is start_of(m), a function of its key alone, and it has no when, so load sees that extra[2026-01] falls
# on 2026-01-01, before from 2027-01-01: the scenario is refused (the base's ask still answers), with L §8.3's
# message (round 9) "move <m> of <s> books on <d>, before <from>", d the first such instance's day.
=== household.tally
model household
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2027-12-31

source plan "plan"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2019-05-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input amt: money PLN
input dom: int

version base
  cite plan
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  amt = 10.00 PLN "own"
  dom = 5 "own"
  opening[konto] = 100.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "wyciąg"

ask b: bal(konto, 2027-12-31)
=== early.tally
scenario early over household
  tally 2
  from 2027-01-01

move extra[m in months]: transfers
  on start_of(m)
  at start_of(m)
  leg cash from konto to world amount amt

ask e: bal(konto, 2027-12-31) in early
=== expect
b: 100.00 PLN
...
e: refused: LOAD-SCENARIO move extra of early books on 2026-01-01, before 2027-01-01 (early.tally:5)
...
